  "remaining": [
    "Route native wheel input/policy to the real native scroll view; current checks cover programmatic offsets and native arrow tracking, not wheel parity.",
    "Qualify long-document caret reveal/autoscroll, pointer text selection/dragging, nowrap and horizontal modes, scroll promises/smooth/scrollend edge cases, CSS zoom, mixed scaling/HiDPI, IME and accessibility.",
    "Bind Firefox native document/clip geometry and scroll ownership to its engine. Its existing experimental native multiline editing still passes but its full viewport remains unfinished.",
    "Resolve Firefox original auto-hidden menu-bar interference after Alt shortcuts. Its independent clipboard fixture still dismisses that menu and focuses the actual browser pane.",
    "Finish other browser frontend controls, dialogs, menus and rich text; audited automatic build selection/installation and actual installed Workspace/PAM deployment.",
    "Qualify Chrome, Vivaldi, Firefox derivatives and other browser versions/architectures, then continue remaining non-GNUstep GTK/Qt/KDE applications."
  ]
